 to participation in various cash generating demand response programs, derate of ASICS due to adverse weather and ASIC maintenance and repair.","context":"(2) Joules of energy required to produce each terahash of processing power","section":"ITEM 2. Management’s Discussion and Analysis of Financial Condition and Results of Operations","block":687,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001083301-26-000166","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-05","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001083301","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1083301/000108330126000166/wulf-20260630.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/8ec2ba174c452e68e621dfe5627aaefadda95d4ab2aeab9afc79ecea0e0e62a9.bin","sha256":"8ec2ba174c452e68e621dfe5627aaefadda95d4ab2aeab9afc79ecea0e0e62a9"}},{"id":"b9368d38a630b1bded0ff035e9034d492c406be887ee838fc7ed9d711a8a577a","quote":"As of June 30, 2026, our operational hashrate represented approximately 0.6% of the total global hashrate, aligning with our share of global blockchain rewards. As of that date, this translated to approximately 1 bitcoin mined per day. To maintain profitably, we focus on optimizing operational efficiency and cost management, ensuring that our mining rewards consistently cover direct operating expenses.","context":"(3) While nameplate at the LMD Bitcoin Mining Facilities was 10.6 EH/s and 12.8 EH/s as of June 30, 2026 and 2025, respectively, actual operational hashrate depends on a variety of factors, including (but not limited to) performance tuning to increase efficiency and maximize margin, scheduled outages (scopes to improve reliability or performance), unscheduled outages, curtailment due to participation in various cash generating demand response programs, derate of ASICS due to adverse weather and ASIC maintenance and repair.","section":"ITEM 2. Management’s Discussion and Analysis of Financial Condition and Results of Operations","block":688,"table":