:{"accession":"0001083301-26-000166","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-05","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001083301","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1083301/000108330126000166/wulf-20260630.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/8ec2ba174c452e68e621dfe5627aaefadda95d4ab2aeab9afc79ecea0e0e62a9.bin","sha256":"8ec2ba174c452e68e621dfe5627aaefadda95d4ab2aeab9afc79ecea0e0e62a9"}},{"id":"b5c93bcf6e7de1f05858a20ec4c07693e11229c54c7381b5dfba18d254fadcbd","quote":"NOTES TO CONDENSED CONSOLIDATED FINANCIAL STATEMENTS (unaudited)","context":"TERAWULF INC. AND SUBSIDIARIES","section":"Segment Reporting","block":233,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001083301-26-000166","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-05","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001083301","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1083301/000108330126000166/wulf-20260630.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/8ec2ba174c452e68e621dfe5627aaefadda95d4ab2aeab9afc79ecea0e0e62a9.bin","sha256":"8ec2ba174c452e68e621dfe5627aaefadda95d4ab2aeab9afc79ecea0e0e62a9"}},{"id":"a886045355f620dda737481b9a816001de2f7acc677bb84ddf731404ddf5cb14","quote":"Prior to the transaction, Beowulf E&D also performed certain administrative services to certain affiliates of the Seller. Concurrent with the Purchase Agreement, the Company entered into a transition services agreement (the “TSA”) through which the Company, along with Beowulf E&D, agreed to provide to certain affiliates of the Seller, who are related parties of the Company due to control by a member of the Company’s management, certain transition services including, but not limited to, services related to tax and accounting, human resources and payroll, information technology, legal, and other general services for a period of two years, unless terminated early in accordance with the provisions of the TSA. In consideration for the services, the Seller affiliates agreed to pay the Company a quarterly fee of $100 as well as reimbursement for third-party expenses incurred in the performance of the services. The Company determined that the TSA is not separate from the business combination and represented additional consideration transferred in the business combination. Accordingly, the Company recorded a liability at fair value at the Acquisition Date of $1.3 million to be amortized over the two-year term of the TSA. The Company had a $0.6 million and $0.9 million liability related to the future services to be provided under the TSA included in other liabilities in the condensed consolidated balance sheets as of June 30, 2026 and December 31, 2025, respectively.","context":"NOTES TO CONDENSED CONSOLIDATED FINANCIAL STATEMENTS (unaudited)","section":"Segment Reporting","block":234,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001083301-26-000166","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-05","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001083301","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1083301/000108330126000166/wulf-20260630.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/8ec2ba174c452e68e621dfe5627aaefadda95d4ab2aeab9afc79ecea0e0e62a9.bin","sha256":"8ec2ba174c452e68e621dfe5627aaefadda95d4ab2aeab9afc79ecea0e0e62a9"}},{"id":"286e6d17f57ad9b0029f771446a87ec73c746e632e2854ef09bd0109ab20656f","quote":"The following table summarizes the Acquisition Date fair value of the aggregate consideration paid for Beowulf E&D pursuant to the Purchase Agreement (in thousands):","context":" agreed to provide to certain affiliates of the Seller, who are related parties of the Company due to control by a member of the Company’s management, certain transition services including, but not limited to, services related to tax and accounting, human resources and payroll, information technology, legal, and other general services for a period of two years, unless terminated early in accordance with the provisions of the TSA. In consideration for