dditional paid-in capital in the condensed consolidated balance sheet.","section":"Segment Reporting","block":272,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001083301-26-000166","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-05","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001083301","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1083301/000108330126000166/wulf-20260630.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/8ec2ba174c452e68e621dfe5627aaefadda95d4ab2aeab9afc79ecea0e0e62a9.bin","sha256":"8ec2ba174c452e68e621dfe5627aaefadda95d4ab2aeab9afc79ecea0e0e62a9"}},{"id":"aea68d18eb11ab4900959a95452a80e4c9f6c45cc25397b8e944b8882396eee6","quote":"NOTES TO CONDENSED CONSOLIDATED FINANCIAL STATEMENTS (unaudited)","context":"TERAWULF INC. AND SUBSIDIARIES","section":"Segment Reporting","block":275,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001083301-26-000166","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-05","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001083301","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1083301/000108330126000166/wulf-20260630.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/8ec2ba174c452e68e621dfe5627aaefadda95d4ab2aeab9afc79ecea0e0e62a9.bin","sha256":"8ec2ba174c452e68e621dfe5627aaefadda95d4ab2aeab9afc79ecea0e0e62a9"}},{"id":"f879ab3206695ecd70bebc202172971b047bd0446783742a864a17a9e94d7cf3","quote":"On May 22, 2026, the Company, through a wholly owned subsidiary, acquired 100% of the membership interests of IEP, which owned or had the contractual purchase rights to approximately 308 acres of land located in Grayson, Kentucky under a pre-existing land purchase agreement. The acquisition was accounted for as an asset acquisition as the acquisition involved the purchase of land with an option to purchase additional acreage. Accordingly, the total cost of the acquisition including directly attributable transaction costs, was allocated to the acquired assets on a relative fair value basis. The acquisition expanded the Company’s portfolio of large-scale, energy-advantaged digital infrastructure campuses and advanced the Company’s strategy of developing shovel-ready AI and HPC sites with long-term power availability and robust transmission infrastructure.","context":"Muskie Data Campus","section":"Segment Reporting","block":277,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001083301-26-000166","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-05","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001083301","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1083301/000108330126000166/wulf-20260630.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/8ec2ba174c452e68e621dfe5627aaefadda95d4ab2aeab9afc79ecea0e0e62a9.bin","sha256":"8ec2ba174c452e68e621dfe5627aaefadda95d4ab2aeab9afc79ecea0e0e62a9"}},{"id":"eef086d2300db00113d1833365e8c292d23054b31a4963183fb2d50995f81e6c","quote":"Total consideration for the Muskie Data Campus asset acquisition consisted of (i) $30.0 million in cash paid at closing, (ii) $50.0 million of deferred cash consideration due on the first anniversary of closing, and (iii) contingent consideration of up to $90.0 million, determined at $90,000 per MW of power capacity delivered to the Muskie Data Campus under an agreement with Kentucky Power Company, up to a maximum of 1,000 MW due upon achievement of the applicable milestones, and only to the extent the milestones are achieved within 15 years following closing. The Company determined that payment of the $90.0 million was probable and recognized this amount as a component of the cost of the acquired assets and is included within other liabilities in the condensed consolidated balance sheet as of June 30, 2026.","context":"On May 22, 2026, the Company, through a wholly owned subsidiary, acquired 100% of the membership interests of IEP, which owned or had the contractual purchase rights to approximately 308 acres of land located in Grayson, Kentucky under a pre-existing land purchase agreement. The acquisition was accounted for as an asset acquisition as the acquisition involved the purchase of land with an option to purchase additional acreage. Accordingly, the total cost of the acquisition including directly attributable transaction costs, was allocated to the acquired assets on a relative fair value basis. The acquisition expanded the Company’s portfolio of large-scale, energy-advantaged digital infrastructure campuses and advanced the Company’s strategy of developing shovel-ready AI and HPC sites with long-term power availability and robust transmission infrastructure.","section":"Segment Reporting","block":278,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001083301-26-000166","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-05","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001083301","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1083301/000108330126000166/wulf-20260630.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/8ec2ba174c452e68e621dfe5627aaefadda95d4ab2aeab9afc79ecea0e0e62a9.bin","sha256":"8ec2ba174c452e68e621dfe5627aaefadda95d4ab2aeab9afc79ecea0e0e62a9"}},{"id":"8e5a8387bbbf301b26fc33e9be0ac69a41623ff278271bbbeb6adbdd2a2d2cf0","quote":"The Company may also be required to pay additional contingent consideration of up to $50.0 million, determined at $100,000 per MW of power capacity contracted under future data center lease agreements, up to a maximum of 500 MW in excess of the 1,000 MW discussed above. This contingent payment becomes due upon achievement of the applicable milestone, and only to the extent the milestone is achieved within 15 years following closing. As of June 30, 2026, the Company has not recognized the additional contingent consideration as the underlying contingency was deemed not yet probable.","context":"Total consideration for the Muskie Data Campus asset acquisition consisted of (i) $30.0 million in cash paid at closing, (ii) $50.0 million of deferred cash consideration due on the first anniversary of closing, and (iii) contingent consideration of up to $90.0 million, determined at $90,000 per MW of power capacity delivered to the Muskie Data Campus under an agreement with Kentucky Power Company, up to a maximum of 1,000 MW due upon achievement of the applicable milestones, and only to the extent the milestones are achieved within 15 years following closing. The Company determined that payment of the $90.0 million was probable and recognized this amount as a component of the cost of the acquired assets and is included within other liabilities in the condensed consolidated balance sheet as of June 30, 2026.","section":"Segment Reporting","block":279,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001083301-26-000166","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-05","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001083301","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1083301/000108330126000166/wulf-20260630.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/8ec2ba174c452e68e621dfe5627aaefadda95d4ab2aeab9afc79ecea0e0e62a9.bin","sha256":"8ec2ba174c452e68e621dfe5627aaefadda95d4ab2aeab9afc79ecea0e0e62a9"}},{"id":"ea2f63832aeeb04dfabe6ab09b9acd6c22d654cd8bb1946561178f502a551e1f","quote":"The following table summarizes the costs of the acquisition of the Muskie Data Campus (in thousands):","context":"The Company may also be required to pay additional contingent consideration of up to $50.0 million, determined at $100,000 per MW of power capacity contracted under future data center lease agreements, up to a maximum of 500 MW in excess of the 1,000 MW discussed above. This contingent payment becomes due upon achievement of the applicable milestone, and only to the extent the milestone is achieved within 15 years following closing. As of June 30, 2026, the Company has not recognized the additional contingent consideration as the underlying contingency was deemed not yet probable.","se